Negative control for a header sorting only what its own column IS (R6-6b).

Falls a column with no declared ordering back to the collection's default wire
field, so EVERY header — the status composite and the bounce date the enum has
no column for — draws a sort control, and clicking any of them orders by
`default`. A header that says one thing and orders by another.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the header-affordance spec — only a column that declares a real sort
field carries a sort control; the composite and the undeclared date column draw
a plain header.

